    "terrainName": "bt-range",
    "description": "What: a flame tank burns the men in a building THROUGH ITS OPENING (CE-3486 flame FL-2, R-3111; docs/designs/weapons/DESIGN_Flame_Weapons.md F-2, F-11): the drill puts the flame INTO the window, it does not need to see who is inside. On bt-range the 'CQB House' (one storey, its west wall at x 40, its room-C window at y 101.25..102.75 over a 0.9 m sill) holds two unarmed hostiles: 'Defender A' in room C at (44, 102), on the window's line, and 'Defender At Wall' just inside the west wall at (41.5, 103.6) - inside the jet's 5 degree cone, but with the wall, not the window, on his line from the turret. 'Flame Tank' (the M67, friend) stands 28 m west, ordered FireAtPoint with its flamethrower (mount 0) at the window, 60 fuel shots (6 s). Judge: the tank spends fuel (no round); Defender A is set alight through the window, burns and dies; Defender At Wall never burns (the wall stops the flame, the opening passes it)."
  },
